- Manual muscle testing of right vs. left lower extremity (hip flexion, knee extension, ankle dorsiflexion, plantar flexion) graded on 0–5 scale;  
- Sensory testing to light touch and pinprick in dermatomal pattern (L2–S2), noting any level or asymmetry;  
- Patellar and Achilles reflexes (graded 0–4+);  
- Gait observation (trendelenburg, foot drop, ataxia);  
- Palpation of thoracic and lumbar spine for midline tenderness or step-offs.

